-- **Strengths:** Simple to implement, effective for uniform regions (e.g., Minecraft terrain), reduces draw calls significantly.
-- **Limitations:** Only works on 2D planes (requires pre-culling or slicing for 3D volumes), greedy approach may not find globally optimal mesh (though it finds maximal rectangles locally), relies on efficient callbacks.
-- **When to use:** When generating meshes for 2D tile-based games or pre-culled 2D slices of 3D voxel data where draw call reduction is critical.
-- **When not to use:** When global mesh optimization is required, or when the data is not naturally grid-aligned or tile-based.
